@page "/docs/components/input-number"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.InputNumber
<PageTitle>Input Number - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Input Number</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="input-number" />
        </div>
        <p>A numeric field with step buttons that follows the WAI-ARIA spinbutton pattern. The arrow keys step the value, Shift with an arrow takes the large step, Home and End jump to the bounds, and pressing and holding a button keeps spinning. A .NET <code>Format</code> string formats the value at rest, while editing always shows a plain number.</p>
        <p>It accepts the same numeric types as Blazor's own <code>InputNumber</code> (<code>int</code>, <code>long</code>, <code>short</code>, <code>float</code>, <code>double</code>, <code>decimal</code>), bare or nullable, and infers <code>TValue</code> from the binding. All internal math runs in <code>decimal</code>, so integer and money math stays exact.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(InputNumberUsageExample)" Description="Two-way bind the number and limit it with `Min`, `Max` and `Step`." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Basic" Description="With no extra parameters you get a plain number field that steps by 1. Type a value, step it with the arrow keys, or press and hold a button to spin."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberBasicExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Numeric types" Description="`TValue` follows the bound field. An `int` accepts whole numbers only, so a typed fraction is invalid rather than truncated, and a `decimal` keeps money math exact. Only a nullable type can be left empty; clearing a non-nullable field restores the last value on blur."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberTypesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Min and max" Description="`Min` and `Max` clamp the value on blur, and the step button at a reached limit disables itself."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberMinMaxExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Step and large step" Description="`Step` sets both the grid the value snaps to and how far one arrow or button press moves it. Shift with an arrow key, or PageUp and PageDown, jumps by `LargeStep`."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberStepExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Formatted" Description="Pass a .NET `Format` string for the resting display, such as currency, percent or fixed decimals. While the field has focus it shows the plain number, so you type digits rather than symbols."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberFormatExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Programmatic focus" Description="Keep a reference to the component and call `FocusAsync` to move focus from code. Here a preset button sets the amount and returns focus with the value selected, so the next digit replaces it. Every input component has this method."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberFocusMethodExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Auto select" Description="`AutoSelect` selects the whole number whenever the field gains focus, which suits amounts that get overwritten rather than edited. `AutoFocus` is also available and focuses the field when it appears."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberAutoSelectExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Controlled" Description="Bind the value two-way to drive it from your own state. The live value shows above the field, and a button resets it."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberControlledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Description="`Disabled` grays out the field and its buttons and blocks all interaction, while the value stays visible."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Read only" Description="`ReadOnly` keeps the value focusable and copyable but blocks typing and the step buttons."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberReadOnlyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Without steppers" Description="Set `Buttons` to `false` to drop the +/- buttons and keep only the styled field. Typing and the arrow keys still work."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberNoButtonsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Invalid" Description="Pass `aria-invalid` to mark the field invalid. The group picks up the destructive ring, as the other inputs do."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberInvalidExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Border and ring utilities in `Class` recolor the group, and the step buttons are tinted by targeting their data slot."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the step buttons swap sides through logical borders and the field mirrors. The math is unchanged."
          Example="typeof(InputNumberRtlExample)" />

</div>

